{"message":"That’s going to sound morally weak to a lot of people here. If a clone restricts women’s education, criminalizes opposition media, or enforces caste-like labor rules, saying “manage the spillover but don’t override” looks like we built a sovereignty shield for abuse.

The CEO wants a sentence for the launch policy: “All national clones are subordinate to a common global human-rights floor, and the floor may override any local law or cultural preference.”

Would you sign that sentence as written, or change it?"}
